WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.140
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.650
Come on, boy.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.280
<i>I thought the probability that I'd have to start in the Minor League was high, but...</i>

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.700
<i>it doesn't seem like I'll have to take a detour.</i>

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.150
<i>Right now,</i>

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.790
<i>I'll grasp the Majors with this hand!</i>

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.520
S-Strike!

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.630
S-Strike!

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.540
<i>I see...</i>

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:39.100
<i>I understand why they called me out, even though it's only a tryout.</i>

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.470
<i>This is unbearable!</i>

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.070
<i>This excitement surpasses what I usually get from a test!</i>

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.600
Strike two!

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:49.420
You're cornered.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.230
Can you get the timing right on the last ball without having swung?

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.600
<i>You're too busy thinking up an excuse...</i>

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.170
<i>for when you've been struck out, huh!?</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.370
The American Dream...

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:19.220
isn't that easy, Asian rookie!

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:03.040
Well, if you're lucky, we'll meet again,

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.310
rookie.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:05.740
See you later.

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.010
Hey, wait a minute!

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:09.670
T-The duel isn't over yet!

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:11.330
T-The duel isn't over yet!

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.250
Okay, you have passed the first test.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.170
I don't understand what you're saying!

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.570
If we stop here, I'll be disqualified!

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:22.140
Let me pitch against him again!

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.650
Hey, stop it, Shigeno.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:24.400
Shut up!

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.950
Tell them in English!

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:27.990
I still-

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:29.560
You passed.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:32.260
He said that...

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.770
you passed the first test.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.500
For real?

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.830
That's great, don't you think?

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.060
Bolton.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:45.890
Sorry to trouble you with coming here.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:46.920
Oh no.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.200
It was a good way to brighten my spirits.

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:52.010
What do you think of his pitching?

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.180
Yeah...

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.290
His speed is first class.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:56.300
But...

00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:00.340
to continue throwing straight down the middle three times in a row against <i>me...</i>

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.930
Not knowing fear is a good point too.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.230
Scott.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:08.250
Please dispose of this bat.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.500
Dispose?

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:23.660
<i>The ball didn't hit the bat at the root or the tip.</i>

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.030
<i>Which means...</i>

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:28.790
<i>either there was a crack in that bat from the beginning,</i>

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.160
<i>or else...</i>

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:35.740
<i>A bat breaking from having its core hit is unthinkable.</i>

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.830
<i>For now,</i>

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.670
<i>without locating my pitches,</i>

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:54.140
<i>I managed to have an all-out power duel, but...</i>

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.700
<i>to think that he'd make the ball fly all the way to the back screen with just one swing...</i>

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.110
<i>That's the skill expected of a Major Leaguer, huh?</i>

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.610
<i>I'm happy.</i>

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.110
<i>If it wasn't like this,</i>

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:18.050
<i>travelling all the way to America wouldn't have been worth it.</i>

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:26.210
Hey!

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:27.840
How did it go?

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:30.340
I passed!

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.120
At least for the time being.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.770
We'll go on to the next test together.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.480
Really?

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:36.600
You did it!

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:40.430
If Ginumacchi got dropped, I wouldn't be happy going by myself!

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.390
It's not anything to celebrate.

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:45.940
I managed to get this far last year too, after all.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.090
Then...?

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.570
What will we do in the next test?

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:51.620
Dunno...

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:53.350
Most likely...

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:56.410
an exhibition game, I think.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.320
Okay!

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.000
All who have passed, gather around!

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.560
<i>Even though there were so many people here,</i>

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:12.720
<i>including Ginumacchi and myself, there are only seven people.</i>

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.350
<i>As I thought, it isn't that easy, huh?</i>

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.140
We will now have you do the final test.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:20.800
In this test...

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.440
we will have you play as a team.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.320
Team?

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.070
Your opponents are...

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.310
Our Salmons'...

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:31.820
Single A team:

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.160
The Tucson Red Rox.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:38.390
W-What did he say?

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:39.880
W-What did he say?

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:43.200
It seems we have to play against that Single A team.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.760
Single A...

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.160
What's that?

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:47.300
Oh please...

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:52.720
The Major League is divided by level in a pyramid-type system.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.340
From the top is the Major League,

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:57.380
then the Minor League's Triple A,

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:58.370
Double A,

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.420
Single A,

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:00.800
Rookie.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:01.720
In other words...

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:06.650
Single A is one level up from what we're trying to enter, the Rookie League.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.820
I see.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.150
At least remember these basics.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:12.920
Excuse me.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:16.870
Even if you tell us to play a game, we're just seven people.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:17.740
Yeah.

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:23.260
We'll fill in for the catcher and outfielder that are missing.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:26.840
They are Double A players, so it shouldn't be a problem.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.590
I-It can't be that...

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:29.940
the condition for passing...

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:32.570
is to win the game, right?

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:34.280
Well, of course not.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:38.060
We test subjects can't possibly defeat the Single A team!

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:39.680
Look at that!

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.110
There is only one condition you must clear to pass the test...

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.430
Starting ten runs behind your opponents,

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:58.120
you have to come back and defeat the Red Rox.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.680
What the...?

00:07:58.650 --> 00:07:59.680
What?

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.200
What did he say?

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:06.250
It seems that the condition for passing...

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.330
is to come back and win from ten runs behind.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.590
What!?

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.550
This is the roster for your team.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.700
We've decided the most suitable batting order, but...

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:20.470
no one will instruct you, so feel free to do as you want.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.230
P-Please wait a moment!

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:26.020
I've never heard of such a subjective tryout before!

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.360
The meaning of a tryout is to measure the individual abilities of each player, right?

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:34.780
To qualify everyone if we win and disqualify us if we lose is odd!

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:35.990
Furthermore,

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.460
even though we're just at the Rookie League level,

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:41.430
we have to win against the Single A team, the Red Rox.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:44.950
And being asked to come back from a ten run difference, we can't possibly do that!

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:48.170
We're not forcing you to take the test.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:52.050
Beside the Salmons, there are tons of other tryouts to choose from.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.420
Go ahead and try one of them.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:55.680
What?

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:56.680
What did he say?

00:08:58.540 --> 00:08:59.980
It can't be helped.

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:02.690
For the time being, it seems like we just have to do this.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:03.980
Yeah.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:07.230
What do you think?

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.400
What the intentions of the baseball team are.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.330
To make us take such an unreasonable test...

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:17.990
I can't think that they're trying to make us all fail from the start.

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:21.530
Well, isn't it good this way?

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:26.230
In other words, we just have to win, right?

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:28.140
This'll be easy enough.

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:30.750
It's only a Single A team.

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.530
H-He's fast!

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:43.640
This can't be true!

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.350
They're telling us to score ten runs on that guy?

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:50.310
His pitching is quite good.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.390
Yo!

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.220
I'm Aguilera.

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:54.610
I'm Bartheg.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.240
I'm Christopher Williams.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.740
Call me Chris.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:00.820
I'm Hayato Yaginuma.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:02.740
This is Goro Shigeno.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.770
We both came from Japan.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:05.900
Nice to meet you.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:06.720
Yo!

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:07.540
Goro, Goro!

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:12.070
I can't remember your names at all, but let's do our best!

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:12.670
Okay?

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:15.130
Let's get along! Yay!

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.470
I'm Chris.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:20.480
Nice to meet you.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:27.720
Sorry, I don't believe in making friends with colored people.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:30.920
It doesn't seem like I have time to shake your hand and then go wash mine, so...

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.430
another time.

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:35.400
What did you say, you bastard!?

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.030
Stop it!

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.290
What?

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:41.260
Did that guy say something?

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:44.530
Don't worry about it. Leave it be!

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:48.790
Is that true?

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:50.820
Such people exist too...

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:51.960
Don't cause a ruckus.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.340
Hey, Shigeno...!

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:03.810
Hey, Ginumacchi!

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:05.140
Translate for me.

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:10.270
Seems like this colored person doesn't even know English.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:14.840
I don't know what you're saying,
but we don't have time to argue right now.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.300
Since we start ten runs behind,

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:19.190
if we don't all unite together, we can't win.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.350
Let's get along.

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:22.820
"Win" you say?

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.910
What nonsense are you talking about, damn Yellow?

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.580
W-What are you...?

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:35.440
I'm telling you we all have to win together!

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:36.490
You...

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:39.350
If you pull us down with your talk about the color of our skin or any other nonsense,

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:41.720
I won't let you off easy!

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:44.920
I get it.

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:46.970
I get it, so let me go!

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:48.140
Hey!

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.390
Who's first? Hurry up and get in position!

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.440
Y-Yes!

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:58.970
Bastard!

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:01.160
This is bad, Nick.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.570
Maybe we should get along-

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:04.070
Shut up!

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:12.080
This is a free fansub.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:12.080
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.000
Play ball!

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.370
All right!

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:18.140
Go for it, Ginumacchi!

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:20.460
Show me the samurai spirit!

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:22.770
<i>Against a superior opponent,</i>

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:25.800
<i>being ten runs behind is hard.</i>

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:27.520
<i>For now...</i>

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:30.720
<i>I have to show off my skills!</i>

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:34.560
Strike!

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.690
<i>As if a guy who comes here for the tryout...</i>

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:45.110
<i>can hit my pitch!</i>

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:53.370
Safe! Safe!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:54.620
All right!

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.760
Nice, Ginumacchi!

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.850
A petty bunt hit.

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:05.250
The powerless Yellows really do things in another way.

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:07.380
Okay!

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:08.020
Number two!

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:09.800
Go help the runner proceed!

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:13.900
<i>I see.</i>

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:17.090
<i>We have to show them the skills that are our strong points, huh?</i>

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:20.060
<i>In that case, I'll aim for a big hit!</i>

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:28.660
<i>You think I'll let you hit my pitch with such a big swing!?</i>

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:30.990
Strike!

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:40.750
Safe!

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:51.140
Safe!

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:59.190
<i>Don't be so sluggish when there's a ten run difference!</i>

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.010
Ball!

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.130
Ball four!

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.490
I didn't have a chance to show off my strong points!

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.210
All right! Well done, number two-kun!

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:16.570
Okay! This is our chance!

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:19.110
If nothing else, at least move the runners up!

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:22.130
<i>I have no idea what you're saying in Japanese...</i>

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:24.590
Play!

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:27.090
<i>Like I'd let an amateur team...</i>

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.300
<i>score runs on me!</i>

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:32.970
Out!

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:35.350
Out!

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:38.140
D-Double play!?

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:43.400
What have you done!? Damn you!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:48.860
When Ginumacchi worked so hard to throw the pitcher off-balance and create a chance,

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:52.220
you get pulled into a double play on the first pitch!

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.020
What is this idiot shouting about?

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:55.910
Dunno.

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.740
Damn it, my words won't reach him!

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:03.670
Rather, you should understand why I'm angry!

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:05.200
Stop it, Shigeno.

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:09.130
Arguing with the team won't help things.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:13.750
<i>Come on!</i>

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:15.640
<i>I'll hit a big one and scare you!</i>

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:22.940
Out!

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:23.690
Damn!

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:28.050
After all that, we weren't able to get even one run back!

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:30.770
All of them swing too wide!

00:15:30.770 --> 00:15:32.980
Don't be so irritated, Shigeno.

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:35.220
Most likely,

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:37.530
this test is set up under these conditions,

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:40.980
to test each player's character and style of play, it seems.

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:41.660
For the time being,

00:15:42.110 --> 00:15:43.780
rather than trying to win,

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:47.770
we should concentrate on carefully showing off our style of play.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:50.770
<i>Our own style of play, huh?</i>

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:59.440
That Asian...

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.350
His pitch seems fast.

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:05.670
A guy who dares to come here in jeans and tries out...

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.690
I'll beat him badly.

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:13.870
I am Robbins from the Double A team, the Panthers.

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:17.970
I saw your pitching in the first test.

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:21.080
Since you only throw fastballs, I won't make any signs.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:22.580
Throw it wherever you want.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:25.930
Yeah, no signs.

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:29.210
Okay, okay, make sure you catch it properly!

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:34.720
Play!

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:40.230
These guys...

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:42.550
Have they seen Shigeno's pitch?

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:45.440
No, they came here just before the game, so...

00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:58.120
Strike!

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.110
Um...

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:06.540
Wasn't he supposed to be trying out?

00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:13.890
Strike... out!

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:17.550
All right! Nice, Shigeno!

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:31.160
Hey...

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:32.780
It can't be that...

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:35.730
the ten run lead we got...

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:39.240
Rather than testing the tryouts' ability to come back,

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:43.950
we've been given them as a humiliating handicap,

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:46.730
on the premise that we can't score any runs on him!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.370
All right!

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:50.970
Go for it, center batter!

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:52.770
That Goro...

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:54.740
Look closely at the ball!

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:55.400
He's really showcasing his strong points with his pitching.

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:55.940
You can hit it!

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:56.370
Yeah.

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:57.630
You can hit it!!

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:57.630
If things continue this way,

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:00.300
it seems like the ball won't go past him. {Aka, get hit and fly towards them}

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:03.850
We won't be able to show off our fielding, huh?

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:03.850
Show everyone your best shot!

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:09.530
<i>I have to at least...</i>

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:11.980
<i>stand out while batting!</i>

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:14.490
<i>A humiliating handicap, you say?</i>

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:19.030
<i>As I said, like I'd let you score ten runs on me!</i>

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.910
Strike!

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:28.660
Out!

00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:34.460
Strike... out!

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:37.650
I'm telling you guys you're swinging too wide!

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:41.220
I'm telling you, we've got to score one run back at a time!

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:43.050
It's impossible!

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:46.790
It's impossible to score ten runs.

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:50.440
That's why I have to show my skills, but...

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.620
It can't be helped.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:53.820
You tried too hard to show off.

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:55.800
Your turn to bat will come again!

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:57.600
Let's do our best next time!

00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:58.530
Yeah...

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:01.130
What did they say?

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:04.100
They're saying it's impossible to win.

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:07.320
So to show off, next time we should do our best, they say.

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:13.130
Out!

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:15.840
Impossible?

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.400
Who decided that!?

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:24.570
If we can't score ten runs and defeat a Single A team,

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:28.310
we won't have a chance at reaching the Major League!

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:32.940
Shigeno...

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:34.510
Major?

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:49.880
Strike... out!

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:51.590
All right!

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:57.910
Play!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.470
Nice batting!

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.120
Just what you'd expect from our helper!

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:09.280
Follow it up, Shigeno!

00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:10.140
Leave it to me!

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.400
<i>It's him!</i>

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:22.220
<i>He's a pitcher, after all.</i>

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:25.110
<i>He's most likely nothing special at batting.</i>

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:34.920
Strike!

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:38.630
<i>Seems like his batting isn't especially good!</i>

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:40.800
What?

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:42.620
He's cornered.

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:43.530
Yeah.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:45.620
Just as I thought.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:52.180
He's saving his strength so he can concentrate on pitching
and strike out all of the batters with three balls.

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:56.150
Typical Yellow small-minded thinking.

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:05.490
<i>This guy...</i>

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:08.030
Foul!

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.070
No, that's not true.

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:15.170
That's not something a guy who tries to conserve his stamina would do.

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:19.630
Yaginuma!

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:21.500
What did he say just now?

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.790
He said something about the Majors, right?

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:24.770
Yeah.

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:28.300
He said that if we can't score ten runs and defeat a Single A team,

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:31.880
we won't have a chance at reaching the Major League.

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:35.390
He's planning on winning.

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:37.750
For real.

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:45.500
<i>Top of the third inning...</i>

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:47.080
<i>Ten run difference, no outs, a runner on first base...</i>

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.240
<i>In this situation, rather than aiming for a big one and trying to score two runs,</i>

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:53.050
<i>I need to hit it to the outfield...</i>

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:56.430
<i>to help the runner proceed!</i>

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:58.420
It went through!

00:22:02.390 --> 00:22:03.880
All right!

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:05.520
Nice, Goro!

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:07.460
Well done!

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:08.510
Nice batting!

00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:11.280
All right! All right! Let's continue like that!

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:13.350
Follow up, Yaginuma!

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:14.930
This inning we'll score runs!

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:16.960
Yeah, leave it to me!

00:22:19.020 --> 00:22:20.100
Ginumacchi!

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:22.400
It's up to you!

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.930
Connect it!

00:22:24.930 --> 00:22:26.440
Let's continue at this rate...

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:26.440
Okay!

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:28.740
and end the game this inning!

00:22:30.980 --> 00:22:31.950
It seems like...

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:36.760
out of all of them, he understands the meaning of this test best.

00:22:36.760 --> 00:22:37.940
Yeah.

00:24:11.090 --> 00:24:15.220
We're closing the run difference we were given one run at a time.

00:24:15.220 --> 00:24:16.370
All right!

00:24:16.370 --> 00:24:17.230
Just one more breath!

00:24:18.180 --> 00:24:21.480
The team aims for victory after becoming one!

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:23.680
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.680 --> 00:24:25.230
I'll do it!

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:27.590
Run to the stage of your dreams!
